      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "rationale": "A categorical axis capturing a specific service-failure mode directly relevant to explaining negative Yelp experiences; enables grouping and comparison against label_pos. Values are well grounded: YLP-0002's repeated forgetting maps soundly to 'indifferent_slow', YLP-0005's discriminatory refusal to 'rude', and positive reviews correctly to 'not_present'. Categories are non-trivial and provide real analytical leverage."
    },
    {
      "name": "food_taste_or_flavor_problem",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "rationale": "Distinct axis (food quality vs. service) that is a plausible driver of negative experiences, supporting grouping and modeling. Sampled values are sound: positive food reviews correctly 'not_present', and no observed contradictions. Presence of both '<NULL>' and 'not_present' is slightly untidy but does not indicate hallucination; silent rows receiving non-committal values is correct behavior."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
  "source_groundedness": 0.88,
  "rationale": "Both added columns introduce genuine, distinct analytical axes (service failure and food-quality failure) that are directly useful for explaining negative Yelp experiences and can be cross-tabulated with label_pos. Sampled produced values are well-grounded readings of the source text with no observed hallucinations; silent rows are reasonably marked as not present. Judged only on usefulness and groundedness, this is a strong set."
}

